  "working": "Analyze each statement.\n(A) In standard cell notation, a single vertical line represents the salt bridge. Standard notation uses a single vertical line (|) to separate electrodes and a double vertical line (||) for the salt bridge. Thus a single vertical line does NOT represent the salt bridge; it separates the two half-cells. Hence (A) is incorrect.\n(B) Zinc or magnesium blocks protect a steel hull because they are oxidised in preference to iron. This describes cathodic protection; correct.\n(C) A fuel cell converts the energy of a fuel's oxidation directly into electrical energy while the reactants are fed in continuously. This is correct definition of fuel cell.\n(D) The calomel electrode is a metal–insoluble salt electrode. Calomel (PbO2/Hg/KCl) is a metal electrode with an insoluble salt (PbO2) at its surface; correct.\nThus the statement NOT correct is (A).",
